{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BondWeightIsospinSplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondWeightIsospinSplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.split_is_nn_over_pp_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.split_is_nn_over_pp_swap","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondWeightIsospinSplit.lean#L64-L70","doc":"The split factor is precisely `bondWeight b b / bondWeight a a` — i.e. the\n`nn`-for-`pp` swap, the two shared `pn` bonds cancelling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.triton_helium3_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.triton_helium3_split","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondWeightIsospinSplit.lean#L55-L62","doc":"**Isospin split identity.** The only bond difference between `T` and `³He`\nis a single `pp ↔ nn` swap, so under the inverse-product weight their aggregate\nratio is exactly `(a/b)²` — the degeneracy break a symmetric bond model gives as\n`1`. Requires `a, b ≠ 0` (the traces are nonzero at `q₀`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.helium3Aggregate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.helium3Aggregate","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondWeightIsospinSplit.lean#L50-L53","doc":"Product aggregate of the three bond weights of `³He = (p,p,n)`, whose bonds\nare `{pp, pn, pn}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tritonAggregate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tritonAggregate","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondWeightIsospinSplit.lean#L45-L48","doc":"Product aggregate of the three bond weights of the mass-3 isotope\n`T = (p,n,n)`, whose bonds are `{pn, pn, nn}` (here `a := τ p`, `b := τ n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondWeight","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondWeightIsospinSplit.lean#L42-L43","doc":"Inverse-product (Mayer ideal-gas) bond weight `w(x,y) = 1/(x·y)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}